post.description:
Decide: only the named approver. Picks an option with a rationale, confirms
reversibility, sets the review date (default plus 90 days) and the expected outcome;
a prediction creates its outcome record.

Request a technical brief (or full engineering spec) with its flows and wireframes
from an approved PRD version. Creates the spec request and a draft prd_to_spec run:
estimate and start it like any run (over $50 waits for an owner's approval).

get.description:
The people who asked for the launch's items, each with what they asked (their
words) and Oracle's draft of a personal note. External notes are sent by a person;
Oracle never sends them.

SignedOutEverywhere.description:
Every session signed before ``sessions_valid_after`` is refused, this one too;
every personal API token, every MCP client (refresh tokens included) and the run
tokens of the runs you started that are still going are revoked (AC1).
